Project: AutoDMX — open-source Instagram comment-to-DM automation tool.

Stack:
- Next.js 14+ (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
- Supabase (Postgres + Auth) via @supabase/supabase-js
- Deploy target: Netlify (functions, not Vercel-specific APIs)
- No Redis, no separate worker process — background work happens via
  Netlify scheduled functions / GitHub Actions calling API routes
- All Meta Graph API calls go through a single lib/instagram.ts client
- Never log access tokens or webhook payload contents containing PII
- All Instagram access tokens encrypted at rest (AES-256-GCM) before
  writing to Supabase, decrypted only in-memory when calling the API
- Respect Meta's limits explicitly: 200 sends/hour/account, single
  content block on first private reply after a comment, 24h messaging
  window per contact
- Every API route that touches Instagram must check rate limits via
  the send_queue table before calling Meta's API directly